-- Row il-68. EXPECTED RED: the assertions that fail on purpose. Each says that what a citing text points at is there in the target as the instruments print it, and each is FALSE.
-- Four assertions: I1 (one), I2 (two), I3 (one). The count, four, is declared in check.sh (expected_failed) and in encoding.json (expected_red).
-- If a defect is cured, its assertion turns green and the declared count must go down with it.

§ `Expected red`

-- I1: section 7 has a subsection (a), the letter section 14(2) cites.
#ASSERT `the section as printed has the subsection the citation names` (`section 7 as item 1 of Amendment 19 prints it`) (`citation: section 14(2) names section 7(a)`)

-- I2: section 29A(a) is among the provisions section 1C(a) names; section 29C is among them.
#ASSERT `the list names the provision` (`the provisions section 1C(a) names, as SH 3493 item 2 extended them`) ((`the pointer sentence in section 29A(a)`)'s `the citing place`)
#ASSERT `the list names the provision` (`the provisions section 1C(a) names, as SH 3493 item 2 extended them`) ((`the pointer sentence in section 29C`)'s `the citing place`)

-- I3: the percentage the 2023 instruction quotes equals the percentage printed by Amendment 30, the last Knesset-printed text of section 13B(1) the consolidation's list names before 2023.
#ASSERT `the two percentages are equal` (`the percentage the 2023 instruction quotes`) (`the percentage printed by Amendment 30`)
